        "## Exercise 4\n",
        "For each day (t) in the evaluation window, we compute unconstrained minimum-variance portfolio weights for the two covariance estimators from Exercise 3. The weights are computed as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\omega_t =\n",
        "\\frac{\\hat{\\Sigma}_t^{-1}\\iota}\n",
        "{\\iota'\\hat{\\Sigma}_t^{-1}\\iota},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where (\\iota) is a vector of ones. We compute one set of weights using the high-frequency covariance estimator, $\\hat{\\Sigma}^{HF}_t$, and one set using the Ledoit-Wolf estimator,$\\hat{\\Sigma}^{LW}_t$. The weights are fully invested, but short positions are allowed."
      ],
      "id": "1686d850"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# Exercise 4: Minimum-variance portfolio weights\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "def minimum_variance_weights(cov_matrix):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Compute unconstrained minimum-variance portfolio weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "    The portfolio solves:\n",
        "        min w' Sigma w\n",
        "        subject to 1'w = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    Closed-form solution:\n",
        "        w = Sigma^{-1}1 / (1' Sigma^{-1}1)\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    \n",
        "    sigma = np.asarray(cov_matrix, dtype=float)\n",
        "    ones = np.ones(sigma.shape[0])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Symmetrize to avoid tiny numerical asymmetries\n",
        "    sigma = 0.5 * (sigma + sigma.T)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        sigma_inv_ones = np.linalg.solve(sigma, ones)\n",
        "    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n",
        "        # Fallback in case the covariance matrix is singular or ill-conditioned\n",
        "        sigma_inv_ones = np.linalg.pinv(sigma) @ ones\n",
        "    \n",
        "    weights = sigma_inv_ones / (ones @ sigma_inv_ones)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return weights"
      ],
      "id": "2e12ad79",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
